WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Silo. Linux computers on the devices you own.

00:03.000 --> 00:11.000
An illustrated agent uses the Linux desktop: observe, create a project, and check the result.

00:11.000 --> 00:16.000
Manage local and remote computers together in Silo.

00:16.000 --> 00:21.000
Browse project files. Keep your editor and terminal.

00:21.000 --> 00:32.000
Enable SSH for a computer, copy its address, and save a key. Connect an illustrated coding agent to the project.

00:32.000 --> 00:37.000
Choose GitHub repositories per computer. OAuth access starts read-only.

00:37.000 --> 00:42.000
Scope each secret to its allowed computers and HTTPS domains.

00:42.000 --> 00:47.000
Create a local computer backup and see the saved archive.

00:47.000 --> 00:54.000
Connect a development server's port in Network, then open it in your local browser.

00:54.000 --> 00:59.000
Silo. Give your agents a space of their own. Available for macOS and Linux at silo.amontlabs.com.
